# Norma CMS React — Project Conventions

## Installed stack (minimum versions — do not target older APIs)

Use APIs and patterns compatible with these packages. Never generate code that requires or assumes older major versions.

| Package | Version | Notes |
|---------|---------|--------|
| react / react-dom | ^19.2 | Functional components only; `createRoot`; React 19 APIs OK |
| react-router | ^7.13 | Import from `react-router` — **not** `react-router-dom` |
| axios | ^1.16 | Use shared `api` client from `src/api/client.ts` |
| primereact | ^10.9 | Import per-component (`primereact/datatable`, etc.) |
| primeicons | ^7 | Icon classes via PrimeIcons |
| bulma | ^1.0 | Layout/utility classes (`is-flex`, `button`, `title`, etc.) |
| sonner | ^2 | Toasts via `<Toaster />` / `toast` |
| vite | ^7.3 | ESM (`"type": "module"`), `@vitejs/plugin-react-swc` |
| typescript | ~5.9 | Strict TS; prefer `type` imports |
| eslint | ^9 | Flat config era — do not add legacy `.eslintrc` patterns |

## Project structure

Place new files in the matching folder. Prefer kebab-case for multi-word domain filenames.

```
src/
  api/           # HTTP calls (named exports). One file per domain: role.ts, user.ts
  types/         # Domain types/request/response shapes: role.ts, organization-member.ts
  hooks/         # Data/UI logic hooks (default export). useRole.tsx, useCreateRole.tsx
  components/    # Presentational UI (default export). RoleList.tsx, Auth/
  pages/         # Route-level screens (thin; compose components). Role.tsx, RoleCreate.tsx
  context/       # React context providers
  config/        # App config (e.g. API_URL)
  errors/        # Custom error classes
  router.tsx     # Route table
  App.tsx        # Providers, global CSS imports, shell layout
```

### Feature layering (follow existing Role/User pattern)

1. `src/types/<domain>.ts` — entity, list response, query params, create/update payloads
2. `src/api/<domain>.ts` — thin axios wrappers using `api` from `./client`
3. `src/hooks/use<Name>.tsx` — state, effects, loading/error; call API modules
4. `src/components/<Name>.tsx` — PrimeReact + Bulma UI; consume hooks
5. `src/pages/<Name>.tsx` — page chrome + component; register route in `router.tsx`

## Coding patterns

- **API**: named exports (`getRoles`, `createRole`); return `data` from axios; type with generics.
- **Hooks**: default export; `useState`/`useEffect` with cancellation flags for async; Spanish user-facing error strings (match existing UI).
- **Components/pages**: default export; functional components.
- **Routing**: wrap authenticated pages in `ProtectedRoute`; guests in `GuestRoute`.
- **UI**: PrimeReact for tables/forms/inputs; Bulma for layout and buttons/links. Do not introduce another UI kit or CSS framework.
- **Styles**: global Bulma/PrimeReact in `App.tsx`; optional `*.module.css` next to a component when needed.
- **Imports**: relative paths within `src/` (as the codebase does today). Prefer `import type` for types.

## Anti-patterns

- Do not use `react-router-dom` imports or v5/v6-only APIs when v7 equivalents exist.
- Do not add React Query/SWR/Redux unless explicitly requested — hooks + local state is the pattern.
- Do not put API calls or heavy logic in pages; keep pages thin.
- Do not invent parallel folders (`services/`, `stores/`, `features/`) — extend the existing layout.
